## Review Checklist (for outline reviewer)

### Completeness
- [ ] Goal and acceptance criteria are specific and verifiable
- [ ] Steps decompose naturally into test → implement → refactor
- [ ] All steps are independently testable (no hidden dependencies)
- [ ] Step granularity is appropriate (not too broad, not too narrow)

### Risk Coverage
- [ ] All significant assumptions are stated
- [ ] Edge cases are enumerated
- [ ] Rollback plan is stated
- [ ] External dependencies (API, DB, env) are named

### Scope Quality
- [ ] Existing code to reuse is identified with specific paths
- [ ] Out of scope items prevent scope creep
- [ ] Change surface matches the acceptance criteria

### Review Priority
<!-- Keep one: -->
- [ ] **Low** — minor clarification needed, straightforward to implement
- [ ] **Middle** — standard review, a few design decisions to discuss
- [ ] **High** — complex change, careful review required

